= common failoing of semantic =
====== short ======

====== related to ======
https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/dynamic-semantics/

= main =
We consider a situation in which a sentence might have different
<q>meanings</q>. In this condition or in this context this sentence is true (or
better yet grammatical) but in this context the setnece is clearly false (or
better yet ungrammatical)

One, purely lingusitic change of context is exemplified by the first example
from the article:
https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/dynamic-semantics/

    Mary met a student yesterday. He needed help.

In this (somehow annoyingly trivial) example the meaning of <q>He needed
help.</q> depends upon its context which includes the sentence preceeding it.
Another only half remembered example was <q>He passed the ball forwards</q>
or something similar - was it the different meanings of passed, and the specific
standard in the context of rugby - or was it aome jargon term of soccer which
changes meaning in context.

We then invent a theory of semantics AND OF HIDDEN SEMANTIC STRUCTURE (or in the
case of <q>dynamic semantics</q> a hidden process).

It reminds me of the Dalai Lama's rejection of psychotherapy - on the grounds
that it sometimes leaves out what happens in a past life. The problem isn't
caused by just what has happened to this body/life, and if you only look there
you are unduly restricting yuour attention. Now obviously I don't beleive in
re-incarnation (or at least not in a way that what happened in a previous life
can affect ones


There is a reasonable gounds to insist that syntax, and the mapping from syntax
to parse tree, or other semantic structures should be decidable.


There is more fittin into existing theory. and that theory is too rich to be
captured in the semantic structure of the de-contextualised sentence.

The is dea that we can come up with the (or even a) semantic structure which has
this meaning in this context and that meaning in that context and that the job
will be done when every way it unpacks in every context is accounted for (or
nver done becasue it can never be accounted for) is a silly and unhelpfully
distracting theory.

This way does not lie wisdom but trivia.

